      "message": "**Summary:**\n\n\n* **Issue:** The commit message explicitly states: *\"use M_GPR for general-purpose registers (ra, a0-a7, t0-t6).\"* However, in `zephyr/shim/src/panic.c`, the macro for `ra` remains unchanged, using `M(ra, riscv.regs[29], ra)`. Furthermore, in the test code (`zephyr/test/hwtest/src/panic.c`), `ra` is explicitly flagged with `.is_gpr \u003d false`.\n* **Analysis:** The code implementation itself is correct and preferred. Retaining the Return Address (`ra`) register rather than zeroing it out is crucial for identifying the source of the panic during crash analysis. It is only the commit message that is flawed.\n* **Remediation:** Amend the commit message to accurately reflect the code. Remove `ra` from the list of registers being stripped.\n* *Suggested wording:* \"Update the RISC-V PANIC_REG_LIST macro in the Zephyr panic shim to use M_GPR for general-purpose registers (a0-a7, t0-t6). The return address (ra) remains unstripped (using M) to preserve traceback capabilities.\"",
